{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Run a test’s body with a fresh tracker and check the events it tracked, in order."}],"sections":[],"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Recording-a-bodys-events","identifiers":["doc:\/\/TrackerTesting\/documentation\/TrackerTesting\/withRecordingTracker(_:)-8blfh","doc:\/\/TrackerTesting\/documentation\/TrackerTesting\/withRecordingTracker(_:)-mlec","doc:\/\/TrackerTesting\/documentation\/TrackerTesting\/withRecordingTracker(_:)-26pul","doc:\/\/TrackerTesting\/documentation\/TrackerTesting\/withRecordingTracker(_:)-pnmv"],"title":"Recording a body’s events"},{"anchor":"Reading-what-was-tracked","identifiers":["doc:\/\/TrackerTesting\/documentation\/TrackerTesting\/TrackerRecording"],"title":"Reading what was tracked"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/trackertesting"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"type":"heading","anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"withRecordingTracker","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" makes a tracker, binds it to the current task with ","type":"text"},{"code":"withTracker","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" for the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"length of its body, then finishes it and returns a ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/TrackerTesting\/documentation\/TrackerTesting\/TrackerRecording","type":"reference"},{"text":" of every event tracked","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"through it. Each call makes its own tracker, so tests that run at once never see each other’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"events. Events tracked after the body returns, by work it started but didn’t wait for, are dropped.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"There are four spellings. The body can be synchronous or asynchronous, and it can take the tracker","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"tex